      "text": "To determine how many books Melvin has left over after repacking them into boxes containing 40 books each, we need to perform a step-by-step calculation.\n\nFirst, calculate the total number of books in the warehouse:\n\\[\n1335 \\text{ boxes} \\times 39 \\text{ books per box} = 52065 \\text{ books}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to determine how many full boxes of 40 books each can be made from 52065 books. To do this, we divide the total number of books by 40:\n\\[\n52065 \\div 40 = 1301 \\text{ R } 25\n\\]\nThis division tells us that 1301 full boxes of 40 books each can be made, with a remainder of 25 books. Therefore, after packing these full boxes, the number of books left over is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{25}\n\\]",
