      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine how many books Melvin will have left over after repacking them into boxes of 40, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of books:**\n   Each box contains 39 books, and there are 1335 boxes.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total number of books} = 1335 \\times 39\n   \\]\n   To find the product, we can use the distributive property:\n   \\[\n   1335 \\times 39 = 1335 \\times (40 - 1) = 1335 \\times 40 - 1335 \\times 1\n   \\]\n   Calculate each term separately:\n   \\[\n   1335 \\times 40 = 53400\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1335 \\times 1 = 1335\n   \\]\n   Subtract the second term from the first:\n   \\[\n   53400 - 1335 = 52065\n   \\]\n   So, the total number of books is 52065.\n\n2. **Determine how many full boxes of 40 books can be made:**\n   To find out how many full boxes of 40 books can be made, we divide the total number of books by 40:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of full boxes} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{52065}{40} \\right\\rfloor\n   \\]\n   Perform the division:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{52065}{40} = 1301.625\n   \\]\n   The integer part of the division is 1301, so the number of full boxes is 1301.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of books left over:**\n   To find the number of books left over, we multiply the number of full boxes by 40 and subtract this product from the total number of books:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Books left over} = 52065 - (1301 \\times 40)\n   \\]\n   Calculate \\(1301 \\times 40\\):\n   \\[\n   1301 \\times 40 = 52040\n   \\]\n   Subtract this from the total number of books:\n   \\[\n   52065 - 52040 = 25\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of books left over after repacking is \\(\\boxed{25}\\).",
