      "text": "We start by determining the total number of books in the warehouse, which is given by the product of the number of boxes and the number of books per box. There are 1335 boxes, and each box contains 39 books. Therefore, the total number of books is:\n\n\\[ 1335 \\times 39 \\]\n\nTo find the product, we can use the distributive property of multiplication:\n\n\\[ 1335 \\times 39 = 1335 \\times (40 - 1) = 1335 \\times 40 - 1335 \\times 1 \\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\n\\[ 1335 \\times 40 = 53400 \\]\n\\[ 1335 \\times 1 = 1335 \\]\n\nSubtracting these values gives:\n\n\\[ 53400 - 1335 = 52065 \\]\n\nSo, the total number of books in the warehouse is 52065. Next, we need to determine how many complete boxes of 40 books each can be made from these books, and how many books will be left over. This can be found by dividing 52065 by 40 and finding the quotient and the remainder.\n\nPerforming the division:\n\n\\[ 52065 \\div 40 = 1301 \\text{ R } 25 \\]\n\nThis means that 52065 divided by 40 gives a quotient of 1301 and a remainder of 25. The quotient 1301 represents the number of complete boxes, and the remainder 25 represents the number of books left over. Therefore, the number of books left over is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{25} \\]",
